  "key_findings": {
    "recommended_index": "IVF256,SQ8",
    "recommendation_rationale": "IVF-SQ8 achieves 97.7% recall@10 at 1M scale with 6.2ms/query latency, 4\u00d7 memory savings vs Flat (776 MB vs 3072 MB), GPU-accelerated, and builds in 8.1 seconds. It provides the best balance of recall, speed, and memory efficiency for production deployment.",
    "alternative_for_exact_recall": "IVF256,Flat with nprobe=256 (100% recall, 11.7ms/query)",
    "pq_caveat": "Product Quantization indices showed lower recall (12-17%) on our embeddings. This is expected: PQ performs best when the data distribution is well-aligned with the subspace decomposition. Our DINOv2 embeddings are highly correlated across dimensions, which PQ's independent subspace assumption doesn't capture well. For real production use, OPQ (Optimized Product Quantization) rotation would help.",
    "hnsw_note": "HNSW32 provides excellent recall at small scales (98% at 1K) but build time grows superlinearly (102s at 100K), making it impractical for 1M+ vectors. Also CPU-only \u2014 no GPU acceleration available."
  },
